Up until last night, I'd never read anything by Moorcock.
But I checked alt.binaries.e-book.fantasy last night, and
someone had posted most of the Elric stories there on 11-28,
so I DLed them and started reading.  They should still be
available on most servers for several more days if other
Moorcock/Elric neophytes here wish to DL them.

Wow.  I see now where a lot of the imagery in Nethack
comes from!  Chaoticness, lawfullness, alignment, wariors,
weapons, armor, battles, sorcery, spellbooks, Arioch,
Stormbringer, mazes, dungeons, giant beetles, giants,
etc, etc, etc -- it's all in here.

In fact, I think now maybe 50% of the stuff in Nethack
is from Moorcock, and maybe 30% from Tolkien (dwarves,
hobbits, elves, nazgul, Orcrist, etc.), and the other
20% from other fantasy and myth (vampires, gnomes, etc.).

